WEBVTT

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.240
Yes, hello?

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.880
<i>My name is Nase Izumi.</i>

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.080
Nase? <i>The</i> Nase?

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.320
<i>Yes.</i>

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.410
<i>I'm calling with some news for you.</i>

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.780
Kuriyama Mirai-san?

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.560
Pleased to meet you.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.900
I'm Nase Izumi.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:19.780
This is Kuriyama Mirai.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:23.030
A spirit hunter and legitimate successor of the cursed bloodline.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:28.630
Do you mean the clan that is
shunned by most spirit hunters?

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.540
Yes.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.330
Kuriyama-san.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:44.530
She can use her own blood as a weapon.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:50.650
Not only can it be hardened, it can also be used as a lethal poison that erodes bodily tissue.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.070
Will that be enough?

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.900
It's hard to say.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.150
But I believe she stands a very good chance.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.810
Isn't the target said to be immortal?

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.280
Yes.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:03.880
Immortal?

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:08.510
In truth, he's just terrifyingly quick to recover,

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.710
but he's known to the spirit hunters
around here as the "immortal half-shade."

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.590
The immortal half-shade?

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.210
Let me show you.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:25.520
Unlike shadelings, he's half human and half shade—a preposterous and dangerous being.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:30.310
My research showed me that his shade half resembles the shade beyond the horizon.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:34.720
My younger brother attempted to kill this fellow
but had the tables turned on him.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.930
He nearly died from his injuries.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.400
You're the only one I can count on.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.990
Please.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:48.660
This is the shade from beyond the horizon?

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:53.860
Sorry for dragging you along to
that stifling meeting back there.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:57.490
It may be because of this area's long history, but we have certain customs.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:58.820
Bonsai?

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.960
Yes.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.240
Um, that aside...

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.150
What?

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:05.090
Where's this shade from beyond the horizon?

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.540
Rest assured.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.530
He's under constant supervision.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:11.640
I'll have to kill him sooner or later, right?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.320
Then I'd prefer it to be sooner.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:13.850
Can you?

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.520
How should I know?!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.820
You had no idea either—

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.100
I'm asking you if you're mentally prepared for this.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.670
The half-shade's name is Kanbara Akihito.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.600
<i>Suicide.</i>

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:56.200
<i>Defined in the dictionary as "the act of taking one's own life,"</i>

00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:01.080
<i>it's something I will probably never even think about doing.</i>

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:06.030
<i>Not because I think it's unethical,</i>

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.580
<i>but for a more fundamental reason.</i>

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.240
<i>However, let's save that for later.</i>

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.500
<i>Right now, she's about to die.</i>

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.240
<i>At least, it seemed like that to me.</i>

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:24.540
<i>At this point the story can proceed in one of two ways.</i>

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:30.200
<i>Either the protagonist plays an active role in the events that unfold,</i>

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:36.140
<i>or he takes a passive role as the story moves on without him.</i>

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.690
<i>By all accounts, I'd fall into the latter category,</i>

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.980
<i>but for some reason, I chose the former option at this time.</i>

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.820
H-Hey!

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.580
<i>I won't repeat everything I said, but...</i>

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:58.170
"...at any rate, someone who looks as good in glasses as you

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.630
simply must not die!"

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.000
<i>That was my heartfelt plea to her.</i>

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.220
<i>I finished by screaming out everything I felt at that moment.</i>

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.510
"Basically, I love glasses!"

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.390
How unpleasant.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.030
You—

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:33.150
You picked a fight with the wrong person.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.720
Hey, uh...

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.750
Think you could at least do something about this sword?

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.710
Please?

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:51.620
<i>And that's how I met Kuriyama Mirai.</i>

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.870
<i>If our story had ended after a meeting like that,</i>

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:01.000
<i>I don't think any story in this world would be worth telling.</i>

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:08.360
Beyond the Boundary

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.040
<i>Did she give up?</i>

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.880
Where did you even come from?!

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:35.950
Take this!

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.460
Hey, we can't go around destroying buckets!

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:49.320
Jeez!

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.470
I think it's about time we put an end to this.

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:19.850
What is this, a horror movie?

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.960
E-Everything's dark!

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:25.940
What'd you do to me?!

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.140
It's just a bucket.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.280
Are you hungry?

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:39.950
What's the big deal?

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.160
It's not like you lose anything!

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.520
Of course I do!

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:44.290
You keep chipping away at what's left of my heart!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.690
I <i>told</i> you I still feel pain, didn't I?!

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:48.850
Do you have <i>any</i> idea how much it hurts?

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:52.120
Doing whatever you please to us immortals
is just discrimination!

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:53.470
People are going to hear you, you know.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.960
It's fine.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:56.640
I already made sure no one else was around.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.680
Thanks for waiting.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.520
Here are your extra burrito, mole poblano, and chili con carne combos.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.980
Enjoy yourselves.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.880
You ordered even <i>more</i> food?!

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:07.730
You're being unpleasant.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.280
<i>I'm</i> the one who's finding this unpleasant!

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.960
Not only do you practice on me,

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.010
you even have the nerve to mooch off me for dinner!

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.380
Mooch?

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.160
I thought we had a deal.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.160
I'd refrain from challenging you to any more fights tonight, and in exchange,

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.920
you'd treat me to dinner.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.400
So that means you're going to attack me again tomorrow, I take it?

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.110
Why wouldn't I?

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.600
Kuriyama-san!

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.750
Are you alright?

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:41.670
I'm fine.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:42.760
Just a little anemic.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.520
I <i>was</i> using my blood, after all.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.940
Let's take this to Ayaka-san tomorrow.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.440
I'll come pick you up in the morning.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.210
You shouldn't get too close to me.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:10:00.140
I've unleashed powers I normally keep in check.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:03.910
Immortal or not, you don't want to touch my blood right now.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.870
We still have to do something about that bleeding.

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:10.950
Give me your hand.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.500
I'll do it myself.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:15.920
Come on.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.850
Kuriyama-san, you haven't joined a club yet, have you?

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.100
I don't have time for that.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.100
I can't interest you in the Literature Club?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.100
Why do you ask?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.350
Because I'd love for a beauty with glasses to join.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.860
How unpleasant.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:34.710
Well, it's the club I'm in,

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:36.360
and we only have two real members right now.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.820
Oh, and the other one's a spirit hunter too,

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.840
so I'm sure it'd work in your favor professionally as well.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.310
I'll have to pass.

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:47.000
Huh? Why?

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.250
I don't want to associate with other people...

00:10:55.250 --> 00:11:00.140
I guess his immortality really can't
be dealt with using normal methods.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:00.760
Yes.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.870
You should observe him for a while.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:07.690
Attacking him haphazardly won't get you anywhere.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:08.230
But...

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:13.810
In time, his shade half is sure to surface again,
as it did against Hiro'omi.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.390
Use that opportunity.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.610
Okay.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.350
Also...

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.570
Let me offer you a warning.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:26.680
<i>You'd be better off keeping
your distance from Akihito-kun.</i>

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:29.560
Oh, right.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:30.410
Kuriyama-san.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.420
Y-Yes?

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:34.350
Remember what we talked about yesterday? How about it?

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:37.300
I want to invite her to come visit the Literature Club. Is that okay?

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.590
She says she hasn't joined any clubs,

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.540
and there aren't many other spirit hunters at our school.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:43.800
Besides, she only just got here—

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.930
I thought I refused already.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.730
I'm scared.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:54.370
I'm terrified of taking lives.

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:57.940
Then why don't you quit being a spirit hunter?

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:01.430
If I could...

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:03.860
If I could, I would've done so a long time ago!

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.560
I tried to quit!

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.070
I tried to quit being a spirit hunter,

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:10.200
quit killing dreamshades,

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.040
and live a normal life!

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:16.290
But this cursed blood flowing through my veins is anything <i>but</i> normal.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.180
This power of mine...

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:22.420
The same goes for me.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:33.350
<i>Why would you say that?</i>

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:35.320
<i>Why...</i>

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:40.110
You're an investigator from the Spirit Hunter Association's Observation Bureau?

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:41.170
That's right.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:45.270
I'm Fujima Miroku. Nice to meet you, Nase Izumi-san.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:47.370
So, what is your business here?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.710
The Hollow Shadow.

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:53.000
Dreamshades this powerful don't show up too often,

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.000
so I'm here to observe it.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.250
Dreams mark the way to the underworld.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:04.010
And we call the darkness that lies within them "dreamshades," masses of human resentment

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:09.060
brought to life by the twisted human heart and all of its hatred, envy, and aggression.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:12.370
Dreamshades will continue to exist as long as humans do.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:15.270
So long as we can see them, we will continue to kill them.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.740
Doesn't that make you feel like spirit hunting thrives on the misery of others?

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.780
I see you have some interesting views on the subject.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.490
How so?

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:33.630
Having descended from a long line of spirit hunters
that have been fighting shades since antiquity,

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:35.840
I see shades the same way a farmer sees rice,

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.240
or a fisherman sees fish.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:40.650
It doesn't matter <i>what</i> they are.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:42.120
I see.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.570
May I ask you something?

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:46.550
Go ahead.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:50.050
What are dreamshades to you?

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.060
That goes without saying, doesn't it?

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.060
Monsters, nothing more.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.060
Do I...

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.230
look like a normal person...

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:03.970
to you?

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.070
In my eyes,

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:14.580
you're nothing but a bespectacled beauty.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:25.000
What... the...

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:28.430
The Hollow Shadow?

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.940
Kuriyama-san...

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:41.600
Hurry up...

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:43.820
And stab me!

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.700
It's in a weakened state right now, isn't it?

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:51.580
Chase it out of my body and you'll be able to finish it off!

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.030
But you'll...

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.130
I won't die.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:56.620
I'm immortal, after all.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:03.210
I won't last much longer.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:04.550
Hurry up!

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:05.590
B-But...

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.970
Isn't this what you came here to do?

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:12.360
Didn't you come here telling yourself you had to do this?

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:14.470
Y-Yes, but...

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.770
Then don't falter now!

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:18.780
Killing it won't change anything.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:22.220
Not the blood flowing through your veins, nor the position you find yourself in.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.110
It won't change a single thing!

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:28.400
But you still came here!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.490
So finish the job!

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.860
Don't give in to the Hollow Shadow!

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.910
Otherwise everything you've done
will have been in vain!

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:36.700
Stab me!

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:38.870
I'm immortal.

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:41.710
So...

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.320
So...

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:46.710
live on!

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:48.870
Senpai...

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.390
Unleash your blood.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:14.720
Goodbye.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:57.390
Senpai...

00:16:58.760 --> 00:16:59.370
Hold it.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:02.410
Stay back.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.090
What's wrong with you?

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:16.970
You went up against the Hollow Shadow, you know?

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.030
Didn't you realize this was going to happen?

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.600
Forgive me.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:24.250
I can't guarantee you'll survive this.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.480
I know.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:39.160
You know that Kanbara-kun's a half-shade, don't you?

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:42.130
When his body falls into a perilous state,

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:44.410
his shade half awakens.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:48.790
Basically, this is big trouble.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:23.660
Sen... pai...

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:30.130
The cage!

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.920
He can negate our spirit powers.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:33.010
Ayaka-san!

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:33.710
I know.

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.060
Oh no!

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:58.700
No way.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.160
Nino-san!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.930
This'll only hold him for a little while.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:07.950
Now's our chance!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.360
This isn't working!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.050
He's going to break out!

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.710
<i>Do I...</i>

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:56.670
<i>look like a normal person...</i>

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:58.920
<i>to you?</i>

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.760
<i>The same goes for me.</i>

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:06.880
I'm sorry.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:11.240
I didn't understand a thing about you,

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:13.860
and yet I...

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:16.860
I have to stop you.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:01.650
Kuriyama-san?

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:16.120
I did it again...

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.400
She's...

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:32.270
Senpai.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:35.020
Sorry.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.380
I'm so sorry!

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:51.330
Thanks for the food!

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:56.140
Slow down and savor it.

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:58.590
I feel like I don't have nearly enough blood!

00:21:58.590 --> 00:22:00.480
I need to replenish my iron.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:02.960
Besides, I can't believe this isn't the Hollow Shadow,

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:07.240
Or that it's only worth 200 yen!

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.590
I don't think Ayaka-san would lie, though.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:11.550
Then what's going on?

00:22:13.820 --> 00:22:15.310
How would I know?

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:24.040
Aren't you going to eat?

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:25.150
Nah.

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:29.350
Where are you going?

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:30.290
The restroom.

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:34.210
Hey...

00:22:34.210 --> 00:22:34.540
Yes?

00:22:35.210 --> 00:22:38.790
Do I look like a normal person to you?

00:22:43.150 --> 00:22:44.550
Let's see...

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:48.970
In my eyes, you're nothing but an
ill-mannered guy who's obsessed with glasses.

00:22:54.090 --> 00:22:55.100
What the heck?

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:20.580
I've given it some thought since then.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:22.500
I realized I shouldn't hesitate

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:28.510
and that I have to defeat Senpai—
the shade from beyond the horizon.

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:30.800
But I...

00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:37.560
I don't want to kill Senpai.

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:41.020
I don't want to... kill him.

00:23:44.920 --> 00:23:50.360
I heard that the lull doesn't
actually begin until midnight,

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:56.120
but for some reason, I sense tension in the air.

00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:01.460
It's more stagnant than tense, if you ask me.

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:02.590
Lull, eh?

00:24:02.590 --> 00:24:03.880
The name fits perfectly.

00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:09.380
I should probably walk home
with my little sister right now.

00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:12.090
She's long gone, though.

00:24:12.090 --> 00:24:13.260
Why?!

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:15.090
Because she doesn't want to
walk home with you.

00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:16.230
Why?!

00:24:16.230 --> 00:24:17.470
Because she hates you.

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:18.540
Why?!

00:24:18.540 --> 00:24:20.180
Because you keep acting like that all the time!

00:24:20.690 --> 00:24:25.410
Senpai, I'd better hurry or I won't make it in time for the supermarket's packed meals sale!

00:24:25.410 --> 00:24:27.270
Oh, okay.

00:24:27.270 --> 00:24:28.020
Later!

00:24:29.350 --> 00:24:30.620
Akkey.

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:33.720
Don't take this lightly.

00:24:33.720 --> 00:24:34.860
I'm feeling strangely nervous.

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:38.330
Sounds like love.

00:24:53.470 --> 00:24:55.090
Want a ride?

00:24:55.700 --> 00:24:57.350
I'll give you one.

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:03.100
A lull, huh?

00:25:07.530 --> 00:25:08.730
Why are you here?

00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:12.860
I figured we could talk a bit while I drive.

00:25:17.640 --> 00:25:19.610
Is that a dreamshade?

00:25:19.610 --> 00:25:20.770
Yes.

00:25:20.770 --> 00:25:27.120
Just like the Hollow Shadow, there are many powerful shades that lack a physical form.

00:25:28.190 --> 00:25:34.000
They say this shade was born from all the resentment shown by humans over the years.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:36.730
It is an entity formed from accumulated malice.

00:25:36.730 --> 00:25:43.210
Apparently it'll lead the world to ruin
if left alone, or something.

00:25:45.310 --> 00:25:50.650
This dreamshade, said to be the cause of disease, war, and natural disasters,

00:25:50.650 --> 00:25:54.190
is also commonly referred to as "the one beyond the horizon."

00:25:55.460 --> 00:25:59.410
Thankfully, only a fraction of it has shown up so far—

00:25:59.410 --> 00:26:00.660
not enough to be harmful.

00:26:01.390 --> 00:26:03.700
Why would you tell me this?

00:26:04.210 --> 00:26:09.000
We believe you Nases have the information we need, but you aren't very willing to share.

00:26:09.410 --> 00:26:12.720
So I thought I'd try to get it from <i>you</i>.

00:26:12.720 --> 00:26:15.990
Looks like they haven't told you anything, though.

00:26:16.990 --> 00:26:18.220
Yakiimo.

00:26:20.560 --> 00:26:21.800
It's the truth!

00:26:22.420 --> 00:26:27.230
So, what is being done about this shade from beyond the horizon?

00:26:27.230 --> 00:26:30.650
Do you mean to tell me we Nases have been preparing in secret?

00:26:32.730 --> 00:26:34.400
Do you want to know that badly?

00:26:39.490 --> 00:26:43.620
Does Kuriyama-san have anything to do with
the shade from beyond the horizon?

00:26:44.130 --> 00:26:45.160
Beats me.

00:26:45.660 --> 00:26:48.750
But it would be amusing if it did,

00:26:48.750 --> 00:26:49.460
don't you agree?

00:26:57.140 --> 00:26:58.130
Bro!

00:26:58.590 --> 00:26:59.970
Oh dear.

00:27:05.820 --> 00:27:09.520
You tailed your little sister all the way here?

00:27:09.520 --> 00:27:11.520
It's almost like you have a thing for her.

00:27:11.520 --> 00:27:13.260
How you wound me.

00:27:13.260 --> 00:27:15.040
The "almost like" part was unnecessary!

00:27:21.620 --> 00:27:22.660
What are you after?

00:27:22.660 --> 00:27:25.370
Ask your little sister.

00:27:33.170 --> 00:27:34.670
Onii-chan!

00:27:37.070 --> 00:27:40.260
That was a wonderful display of love for your brother.

00:27:48.240 --> 00:27:51.270
Wh-What the heck?

00:27:52.900 --> 00:27:56.240
Akihito-kun was run over...

00:27:56.240 --> 00:27:57.570
...so why isn't he hurt?

00:27:57.570 --> 00:27:58.670
Huh?

00:27:58.670 --> 00:27:59.330
Oh, well...

00:27:59.330 --> 00:28:01.530
Don't kill us!

00:28:01.530 --> 00:28:03.820
Please, don't kill us!

00:28:04.910 --> 00:28:07.760
Why would you say that?

00:28:28.190 --> 00:28:29.430
Izumi-san?

00:28:31.100 --> 00:28:32.600
You must be worn out.

00:28:35.020 --> 00:28:37.150
Why are you here?

00:28:39.180 --> 00:28:42.530
Get some more rest.

00:28:48.740 --> 00:28:51.100
<i>Thank you for riding with us today.</i>

00:28:51.100 --> 00:28:53.100
<i>This is Hananodera Station.</i>

00:28:53.100 --> 00:28:56.500
<i>Please make sure you have all your belongings.</i>

00:28:59.500 --> 00:29:02.510
The obvious conclusion is that the lull's taking its toll on him.

00:29:02.930 --> 00:29:08.770
But I have a feeling that it severely weakened
not only his shade half, but also his human half.

00:29:08.770 --> 00:29:11.560
Isn't there any way to make him better?

00:29:12.370 --> 00:29:15.980
If he were human or shade,
there'd be several things we could do.

00:29:16.540 --> 00:29:18.880
But Kanbara-kun's a half-shade.

00:29:18.880 --> 00:29:23.110
Frankly speakin', he's such a rare creature that I have no idea how to treat him.

00:29:24.040 --> 00:29:25.500
Senpai...

00:29:29.570 --> 00:29:33.000
How long have Kanbara-senpai and Mirai known each other?

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:35.840
Well, I don't know all the details,

00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:39.250
but they met around when
Mirai-chan came here, I think.

00:29:42.250 --> 00:29:43.510
It's almost time.

00:29:43.510 --> 00:29:45.600
Stay alert, Ai.

00:29:45.600 --> 00:29:46.430
Okay.

00:29:46.770 --> 00:29:48.430
Thank you.

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:51.700
I was lost in thought.

00:29:51.700 --> 00:29:52.810
It's okay.

00:29:52.810 --> 00:29:54.760
That aside, Kanbara-senpai...

00:29:55.810 --> 00:30:00.270
I'm sure they'd let you stay by his side so long as you ask.

00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:05.090
But it's not like I could do anything.

00:30:05.090 --> 00:30:07.150
Even so, you want to stay with him.

00:30:08.850 --> 00:30:11.100
W-Well...

00:30:11.100 --> 00:30:12.550
How unpleasant.

00:30:12.550 --> 00:30:14.830
You don't really mean it when you say "how unpleasant."

00:30:16.250 --> 00:30:17.610
How unpleasant.

00:30:17.610 --> 00:30:19.800
You meant it this time.

00:30:19.800 --> 00:30:21.750
How can you tell?

00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:26.470
Nobody can stop you from staying by Kanbara-senpai's side if you want to.

00:30:26.470 --> 00:30:31.140
I-It's not about staying by his side.
Nothing like that.

00:30:31.140 --> 00:30:32.910
I... just...

00:30:32.910 --> 00:30:35.020
He loves glasses.

00:30:35.020 --> 00:30:37.700
Like I said, it's not like that!

00:30:37.700 --> 00:30:38.810
It's just...

00:30:39.630 --> 00:30:40.940
I feel normal around him.

00:30:41.380 --> 00:30:44.800
I'm part of a clan with a cursed bloodline.

00:30:44.800 --> 00:30:47.700
I've got these abnormal powers.

00:30:47.700 --> 00:30:48.900
But he makes me feel normal.

00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:51.950
He always has, right from the day we met.

00:30:54.900 --> 00:30:56.360
That's good to hear.

00:30:58.790 --> 00:30:59.960
I'm glad you met him.

00:31:06.370 --> 00:31:07.340
How unpleasant.

00:31:08.290 --> 00:31:10.470
Now that one you didn't mean.

00:31:42.830 --> 00:31:43.670
Izumi-san!

00:31:51.780 --> 00:31:53.180
Senpai?

00:31:53.180 --> 00:31:54.180
He's escaped.

00:31:59.240 --> 00:32:02.230
I wonder how Akihito's shade half took over.

00:32:04.360 --> 00:32:11.860
Ayaka-san told me while he was passed out that his human half had also grown extremely weak.

00:32:12.780 --> 00:32:20.120
It must've become even weaker than his impaired shade half.

00:32:20.120 --> 00:32:25.130
And as a result, his shade half
ended up taking over?

00:32:25.130 --> 00:32:26.140
Yes.

00:32:26.140 --> 00:32:31.010
That would explain why he wasn't as strong as usual back there.

00:32:31.010 --> 00:32:33.010
So he escaped instead.

00:32:38.410 --> 00:32:40.390
I'm sorry!

00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:44.520
"No. 135"?

00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:47.560
"Final Score: 83%."

00:32:47.560 --> 00:32:51.880
"She clearly possesses that special something unique to bespectacled beauties,

00:32:51.880 --> 00:32:55.120
but her expression's too forced and unnatural."

00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:56.660
How unpleasant.

00:32:56.660 --> 00:32:58.420
Did you see those boxes over there?

00:33:00.210 --> 00:33:01.760
H-He's a pervert!

00:33:01.760 --> 00:33:05.930
It's depressing to see one of the rare half-shades turn out to be like <i>this</i>.

00:33:05.930 --> 00:33:09.710
I don't think someone who breaks into apartments should be passing judgment on others.

00:33:09.710 --> 00:33:12.000
But this is too much!

00:33:24.930 --> 00:33:26.560
How unpleasant!

00:33:30.290 --> 00:33:32.400
That text you sent me...

00:33:32.400 --> 00:33:33.820
Is it true?

00:33:33.820 --> 00:33:35.000
Yes.

00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:40.280
The lull should impair all dreamshades, even the one from beyond the horizon.

00:33:41.080 --> 00:33:43.660
If you use all of your blood and your entire body,

00:33:43.660 --> 00:33:50.540
you'll be able to draw out Akihito-kun's
dominant shade half without killing him.

00:33:50.540 --> 00:33:56.340
However, that means the shade beyond
the horizon will invade every last inch of you.

00:33:56.840 --> 00:33:59.470
But that'll save Senpai, right?

00:33:59.900 --> 00:34:02.220
You've already made your decision, haven't you?

00:34:03.790 --> 00:34:04.390
I have.

00:34:06.790 --> 00:34:08.560
This is where Akihito-kun is.

00:34:08.560 --> 00:34:10.370
He'll wake up eventually.

00:34:10.370 --> 00:34:14.310
If you truly wish to save him, go there as soon as you can.

00:34:17.480 --> 00:34:18.580
Kuriyama-san.

00:34:19.870 --> 00:34:22.330
Akihito-kun wants you to live on.

00:34:23.180 --> 00:34:25.860
He wants you to kill him and live on.

00:34:25.860 --> 00:34:28.190
I'm certain he feels that way.

00:34:28.190 --> 00:34:29.830
I guess so.

00:34:29.830 --> 00:34:34.210
You're still going to save him despite that?

00:34:34.210 --> 00:34:34.840
Yes.

00:34:35.700 --> 00:34:39.340
I'm sure he'll be upset with me.

00:34:39.340 --> 00:34:44.400
If he finds out I did something like this,
he'll say that I don't understand anything.

00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:46.040
Just like he did back then.

00:34:51.290 --> 00:34:52.900
Serves him right!

00:35:11.560 --> 00:35:12.330
Senpai!

00:35:42.490 --> 00:35:43.620
<i>Hello?</i>

00:35:43.620 --> 00:35:45.080
Where are you right now?

00:35:47.680 --> 00:35:49.520
<i>Right in front of Senpai.</i>

00:35:51.530 --> 00:35:52.580
<i>You're going to kill him, aren't you?</i>

00:35:52.580 --> 00:35:54.590
You're going to kill him, aren't you?

00:35:59.310 --> 00:36:00.220
Yes.

00:36:04.250 --> 00:36:04.970
Hey! Hello?

00:36:04.970 --> 00:36:05.640
<i>Hey! Hello?</i>

00:36:05.640 --> 00:36:06.560
<i>Hello?!</i>

00:36:35.420 --> 00:36:37.410
I forgot he could negate our powers!

00:37:34.570 --> 00:37:37.940
Do I look like a normal person to you?

00:37:39.690 --> 00:37:40.900
Kill him.

00:37:40.900 --> 00:37:42.280
You're going to kill him, aren't you?

00:37:45.700 --> 00:37:46.740
Live on!

00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:19.940
Kuriyama-san...

00:38:25.990 --> 00:38:28.110
Senpai?

00:38:28.110 --> 00:38:29.780
You're awake?

00:38:33.910 --> 00:38:36.250
Oh, so that's what happened.

00:38:36.250 --> 00:38:37.460
Yes.

00:38:37.460 --> 00:38:39.370
You gave us some trouble
after turning into a shade,

00:38:39.760 --> 00:38:42.660
but thankfully nobody got hurt.

00:38:42.660 --> 00:38:44.060
Oh, I see.

00:38:47.270 --> 00:38:50.190
It's probably because of the lull

00:38:50.190 --> 00:38:52.430
that your wounds aren't healing at all.

00:38:53.180 --> 00:38:58.090
They told me you might die
if I attacked you during it, you know?

00:38:58.090 --> 00:39:00.450
I was worried about that the whole time.

00:39:04.490 --> 00:39:06.660
Keep your hands off the wounds!

00:39:06.660 --> 00:39:09.240
They'll heal once the lull passes.

00:39:09.610 --> 00:39:13.130
Don't they say there's no such thing
as good fusion cuisine?

00:39:13.580 --> 00:39:15.710
It's omelette rice!

00:39:15.710 --> 00:39:16.940
Omelette rice?

00:39:16.940 --> 00:39:17.500
Yes.

00:39:18.570 --> 00:39:20.130
Where's the egg?

00:39:20.130 --> 00:39:21.750
Here.

00:39:22.770 --> 00:39:23.500
Boiled?!

00:39:25.050 --> 00:39:26.620
They've been wiped out!

00:39:29.290 --> 00:39:31.760
Wh-What the heck is that?!

00:39:31.760 --> 00:39:33.720
Sakura got it to celebrate your recovery—

00:39:33.720 --> 00:39:35.200
Nobody does that!

00:39:35.200 --> 00:39:38.840
First of all, just because I was unconscious doesn't mean you could go raid my fridge

00:39:38.840 --> 00:39:40.340
or put a pig head inside!

00:39:40.340 --> 00:39:42.930
Don't worry about all that. Just go lie down.

00:39:42.930 --> 00:39:45.360
I'll go shopping and make you a proper one this time.

00:39:45.360 --> 00:39:47.000
Why?

00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:48.250
"Why"?

00:39:48.250 --> 00:39:49.600
Well...

00:39:49.600 --> 00:39:50.600
What's wrong?

00:39:50.600 --> 00:39:51.700
Nothing, it's just—

00:39:51.700 --> 00:39:53.410
You can't even tell?

00:39:53.410 --> 00:39:54.760
Sakura!

00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:55.370
When did you get here?

00:39:56.130 --> 00:39:58.210
She's been taking care of you.

00:39:58.210 --> 00:40:01.090
Mirai hasn't left your side
even once since you collapsed.

00:40:02.580 --> 00:40:04.200
You still don't get it?

00:40:04.200 --> 00:40:04.710
Get what?

00:40:05.270 --> 00:40:07.280
Mirai, I think this guy's a lost cause.

00:40:08.360 --> 00:40:09.790
What are you saying?

00:40:09.790 --> 00:40:10.880
What are you <i>saying</i>?!

00:40:10.880 --> 00:40:12.770
You should just tell him.

00:40:12.770 --> 00:40:13.610
Tell him what?

00:40:13.610 --> 00:40:14.960
Tell him <i>what</i>?!

00:40:14.960 --> 00:40:15.680
What are you two—

00:40:17.300 --> 00:40:18.870
Whoa, it's hot!

00:40:19.600 --> 00:40:22.230
It's summer, after all.

00:40:25.430 --> 00:40:26.940
Summer, huh?

00:40:30.440 --> 00:40:32.500
What? You were here all along—

00:40:32.500 --> 00:40:34.460
Whoa, glasses!

00:40:36.390 --> 00:40:39.740
How strange. Why am I hearing Akihito's voice?

00:40:39.740 --> 00:40:41.160
Am I hallucinating?

00:40:41.160 --> 00:40:42.440
Way to go!

00:40:42.440 --> 00:40:43.830
Even though sunglasses don't have as much—

00:40:45.440 --> 00:40:47.210
Looks like you're the real deal after all.

00:40:48.040 --> 00:40:50.450
You'd better leave at once, then.

00:40:50.450 --> 00:40:55.970
Letting you ogle my swimsuit-clad body for free is humiliating, to say the least.

00:40:55.970 --> 00:40:58.250
Well, I didn't <i>ask</i> you to put it on!

00:40:58.250 --> 00:40:59.210
Jeez.

00:40:59.210 --> 00:41:00.360
Akihito.

00:41:00.360 --> 00:41:00.890
What?

00:41:00.890 --> 00:41:05.150
Learn from this and take a long, hard look at yourself.

00:41:05.150 --> 00:41:09.770
I never want to go through anything like this again.

00:41:13.740 --> 00:41:14.400
Okay.

00:41:14.400 --> 00:41:18.200
Also, drag that pervert over there back to the clubroom with you.

00:41:18.200 --> 00:41:19.410
Hey, pervert.

00:41:20.050 --> 00:41:21.870
What, pervert?

00:41:24.350 --> 00:41:27.410
The days are getting shorter and shorter, aren't they?

00:41:27.410 --> 00:41:29.880
Well, the summer solstice was back in June.

00:41:29.880 --> 00:41:31.370
Want to read some more before we go?

00:41:31.370 --> 00:41:32.460
No.

00:41:32.460 --> 00:41:35.610
Hiro'omi and Mitsuki sure are taking their time.

00:41:35.610 --> 00:41:36.880
They've already left.

00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:37.910
What?!

00:41:37.910 --> 00:41:42.100
Is that any way to treat someone who
just came back from the brink of death?

00:41:42.420 --> 00:41:44.390
Isn't that exactly why?

00:41:44.390 --> 00:41:47.470
I'm sure they just don't know how to face you.

00:41:49.520 --> 00:41:50.650
What's wrong?

00:41:50.650 --> 00:41:52.540
N-Nothing.

00:41:55.940 --> 00:41:57.490
Are you free after this, Kuriyama-san?

00:41:58.720 --> 00:42:01.830
I thought maybe we could get some dinner on the way back.

00:42:01.830 --> 00:42:04.040
Oh, if you're broke, I'll pay.

00:42:04.040 --> 00:42:05.410
R-Right...

00:42:05.410 --> 00:42:10.250
I mean, I don't remember what happened,
but I'm sure I caused you no end of trouble.

00:42:16.360 --> 00:42:19.140
I wish you'd brought it up a little earlier.

00:42:19.140 --> 00:42:19.890
Today's no good?

00:42:19.890 --> 00:42:21.980
No.

00:42:21.980 --> 00:42:25.600
This will probably end once the sun goes down.

00:42:25.600 --> 00:42:27.390
What do you mean?

00:42:29.430 --> 00:42:30.860
Why...

00:42:30.860 --> 00:42:34.860
Why are you so nice to me?

00:42:39.700 --> 00:42:42.530
Because we're kinda similar.

00:42:43.670 --> 00:42:46.000
If I said that, would you get ma—

00:42:46.690 --> 00:42:48.230
Is it <i>that</i> insulting?!

00:42:48.230 --> 00:42:50.390
I-It's not like that!

00:42:50.390 --> 00:42:53.100
You look like you can't stand
the very thought of it!

00:42:53.100 --> 00:42:54.670
D-Does that make you happy?

00:42:54.670 --> 00:42:55.800
Why would it?

00:42:55.800 --> 00:43:03.200
Well, Mitsuki-senpai told me that you
take extreme pleasure in being bullied,

00:43:03.200 --> 00:43:06.220
but I guess it's not that simple.

00:43:06.220 --> 00:43:08.100
I'm glad it isn't!

00:43:08.100 --> 00:43:10.020
Forget everything Mitsuki told you.

00:43:10.020 --> 00:43:11.440
I don't want to!

00:43:11.440 --> 00:43:13.350
I won't forget.

00:43:14.150 --> 00:43:15.700
I won't ever forget.

00:43:20.450 --> 00:43:22.320
What is this?

00:43:23.340 --> 00:43:24.800
It's you.

00:43:25.330 --> 00:43:27.330
The shade beyond the horizon—

00:43:27.330 --> 00:43:32.710
a coalescence of human malice that
they say could lead the world to ruin—

00:43:33.550 --> 00:43:37.220
was the dreamshade within you.

00:43:37.220 --> 00:43:39.090
That's me?

00:43:39.640 --> 00:43:44.720
The whole reason I came to this town was to kill it.

00:43:45.770 --> 00:43:48.560
But that didn't go too well.

00:43:49.540 --> 00:43:52.640
I simply couldn't bring myself to kill you.

00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:54.230
I didn't want to kill you.

00:43:55.060 --> 00:43:55.570
So I...

00:44:05.700 --> 00:44:09.300
When I heard that I could use my blood

00:44:09.300 --> 00:44:13.420
to drive the shade from beyond the horizon
out of you during the lull,

00:44:13.420 --> 00:44:16.500
I decided I had to do it at any cost.

00:44:28.250 --> 00:44:31.440
What happened to you?

00:44:31.440 --> 00:44:32.140
I disappeared.

00:44:33.270 --> 00:44:33.690
Then...

00:44:34.470 --> 00:44:37.300
Then who is this sitting in front of me?

00:44:37.300 --> 00:44:40.190
You haven't regained consciousness yet.

00:44:41.190 --> 00:44:45.380
This is all a dream.

00:44:45.380 --> 00:44:50.950
The little bit of my blood that's still within you
is what's showing you this dream.

00:44:55.340 --> 00:44:57.170
But it's all over now.

00:44:57.170 --> 00:45:00.220
You'll wake up soon.

00:45:00.220 --> 00:45:00.960
Kuriyama-san...

00:45:17.290 --> 00:45:20.500
I thought it'd be easier in a dream,

00:45:20.500 --> 00:45:22.650
but it's harder than I expected.

00:45:24.410 --> 00:45:25.450
Goodbye.

00:45:39.370 --> 00:45:40.620
A dream?

00:45:55.900 --> 00:45:58.120
Good morning, Senpai.

00:45:58.120 --> 00:46:00.110
Quite cold today, isn't it?

00:46:26.230 --> 00:46:27.050
Senpai?

00:46:30.050 --> 00:46:31.580
Senpai!

00:46:36.950 --> 00:46:38.020
Wait.

00:46:38.020 --> 00:46:40.310
Please wait, Senpai!

00:46:41.320 --> 00:46:43.650
Please... wait...

00:47:03.510 --> 00:47:05.050
Kuriyama-san...

00:47:57.610 --> 00:48:02.060
If dreamshades are formed from human malice,

00:48:02.060 --> 00:48:06.320
that makes this a mass of human hatred.

00:48:06.320 --> 00:48:09.070
It's quite fitting...

00:48:09.500 --> 00:48:11.200
for me.

00:48:11.390 --> 00:48:13.450
Three months?

00:48:13.450 --> 00:48:15.830
Yeah. You were in a coma the entire time.

00:48:16.150 --> 00:48:17.490
That long?

00:48:17.910 --> 00:48:19.060
Of course.

00:48:19.060 --> 00:48:21.100
You're no longer immortal.

00:48:21.100 --> 00:48:25.560
You were robbed of the shade beyond the horizon
that was dwelling within you all this time.

00:48:25.560 --> 00:48:27.250
It's a miracle you're alive.

00:48:27.560 --> 00:48:29.190
What the hell?

00:48:29.190 --> 00:48:32.260
So my immortality didn't
come from being a half-shade?

00:48:32.630 --> 00:48:33.830
Probably not,

00:48:34.680 --> 00:48:35.720
Though I'm not sure.

00:48:37.490 --> 00:48:39.740
You should talk to your mother about it.

00:48:40.940 --> 00:48:42.770
So where's Kuriyama-san?

00:48:45.650 --> 00:48:47.610
Kuriyama Mirai's gone.

00:48:48.470 --> 00:48:51.220
She used up all of her blood in a bid to save you

00:48:51.220 --> 00:48:55.130
and took the shade beyond the horizon with her
when she vanished from this world.

00:48:57.360 --> 00:48:59.090
Are you saying she's dead?

00:49:11.290 --> 00:49:14.810
He hasn't eaten anything for
three whole months, after all.

00:49:14.810 --> 00:49:17.000
Anyway, what do you make of this as a dreamshade?

00:49:17.000 --> 00:49:19.720
Akkey says he hears noises coming from the sky.

00:49:19.720 --> 00:49:24.180
The shade inside Kanbara-kun was
the one from beyond the horizon.

00:49:25.390 --> 00:49:29.430
Considerin' how powerful
the shade released from him was,

00:49:29.430 --> 00:49:32.320
ain't it strange he's the only one
who can hear it at all?

00:49:33.080 --> 00:49:36.200
The only plausible explanation is that the shade itself is causing this.

00:49:37.800 --> 00:49:38.370
Hiro'omi.

00:49:38.960 --> 00:49:41.240
Where can I find Izumi-san?

00:49:42.700 --> 00:49:48.270
Only someone from the cursed bloodline could've brought down the shade from beyond the horizon.

00:49:48.270 --> 00:49:49.810
That's all.

00:49:51.870 --> 00:49:53.010
But then we ran into a problem.

00:49:53.890 --> 00:49:56.630
Kuriyama Mirai said that she didn't want to kill you.

00:49:57.450 --> 00:50:00.260
So I reluctantly told her of
a way to save you instead—

00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:04.020
one that would only be effective during the lull.

00:50:04.020 --> 00:50:07.420
Did you really think that explanation would satisfy me?

00:50:07.420 --> 00:50:10.650
Surely you knew she'd pick that option!

00:50:11.900 --> 00:50:13.070
That's right.

00:50:13.070 --> 00:50:14.930
Resent me if you must.

00:50:14.930 --> 00:50:18.660
But as a member of the Nase family,
I was duty-bound to keep everyone safe.

00:50:19.280 --> 00:50:21.410
To keep this <i>world</i> safe.

00:50:21.860 --> 00:50:24.730
Likewise, Kuriyama Mirai also had something she wanted to protect.

00:50:25.960 --> 00:50:27.960
Something she valued more than her own life.

00:50:28.770 --> 00:50:31.470
Something she was willing to die to protect.

00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:35.470
And she did so of her own free will.

00:50:36.190 --> 00:50:38.660
I am indebted to her.

00:50:38.660 --> 00:50:41.600
If she hadn't made the choice she did,

00:50:41.600 --> 00:50:44.970
we wouldn't be here right now.

00:50:45.390 --> 00:50:49.480
In fact, neither would the rest of the world.

00:50:49.870 --> 00:50:54.480
Toward the end, she said you'd probably be
upset with her when you woke up.

00:50:55.130 --> 00:50:57.510
"Serves him right," she said.

00:51:07.990 --> 00:51:10.370
The days are getting shorter and shorter, aren't they?

00:51:11.880 --> 00:51:15.000
I thought it'd be easier in a dream,

00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:17.130
but it's harder than I expected.

00:51:18.760 --> 00:51:19.880
Goodbye.

00:51:23.590 --> 00:51:24.890
What the hell?

00:51:32.030 --> 00:51:34.230
If it's Mirai you want, she never came home.

00:51:34.980 --> 00:51:35.730
Inami-san...

00:51:36.150 --> 00:51:37.240
Where is she?

00:51:41.180 --> 00:51:43.160
Tell me! Where is she?!

00:51:59.280 --> 00:52:00.550
I don't want to see...

00:52:03.120 --> 00:52:06.060
I don't want to see that pathetic back of yours.

00:52:31.750 --> 00:52:35.840
<i>I don't know if this text will reach you.</i>

00:52:35.840 --> 00:52:43.690
<i>Right now, I don't even know if you'll ever get the chance to read this.</i>

00:52:43.690 --> 00:52:45.850
<i>Senpai, Kuriyama Mirai here.</i>

00:52:47.850 --> 00:52:52.240
<i>I'm on my way to see you.</i>

00:52:53.000 --> 00:52:56.540
<i>And then, I'll defeat the
shade from beyond the horizon.</i>

00:53:01.360 --> 00:53:05.110
<i>I'm feeling a little strange right now.</i>

00:53:06.280 --> 00:53:09.290
<i>I actually feel kind of happy.</i>

00:53:10.960 --> 00:53:17.840
<i>Born to a clan with a cursed bloodline,
my life up until now has been anything but nice.</i>

00:53:18.790 --> 00:53:22.220
<i>I always wondered why I was born,</i>

00:53:22.220 --> 00:53:25.460
<i>and some part of me always felt
I was better off dead.</i>

00:53:25.970 --> 00:53:29.120
<i>But I was sorely mistaken.</i>

00:53:30.010 --> 00:53:33.100
<i>Now I'm glad I came into this world.</i>

00:53:33.850 --> 00:53:38.020
<i>My powers were said to be cursed.</i>

00:53:38.020 --> 00:53:40.500
<i>They were despised and scorned.</i>

00:53:40.500 --> 00:53:46.540
<i>However, I now know they were meant not to hurt people, but to save them.</i>

00:53:46.540 --> 00:53:51.200
<i>So I'm really glad I held on
long enough to see this day.</i>

00:53:51.710 --> 00:53:57.440
<i>I'm really glad I came to this town and met you.</i>

00:53:57.440 --> 00:54:03.480
<i>As it turns out, I've been blessed all my life.</i>

00:54:03.480 --> 00:54:05.760
<i>I wasn't cursed at all.</i>

00:54:07.840 --> 00:54:09.110
<i>Senpai,</i>

00:54:10.310 --> 00:54:14.470
<i>now you too can die a normal death one day.</i>

00:54:15.860 --> 00:54:16.520
<i>So...</i>

00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:19.270
<i>So, from now on,</i>

00:54:20.110 --> 00:54:21.890
<i>please live a normal life.</i>

00:54:22.540 --> 00:54:26.590
<i>Just like you told me back then.</i>

00:54:27.210 --> 00:54:29.490
<i>Senpai, I...</i>

00:54:30.490 --> 00:54:33.240
don't feel unpleasant at all.

00:54:51.760 --> 00:54:55.310
Senpai, you should be hiding!

00:55:10.280 --> 00:55:11.700
Senpai,

00:55:13.220 --> 00:55:15.340
I'll...

00:55:16.790 --> 00:55:18.600
I'll protect you.

00:55:54.610 --> 00:55:56.160
What's that thing in the sky?!

00:56:00.860 --> 00:56:01.870
A dreamshade!

00:56:04.160 --> 00:56:05.300
Nino-san?

00:56:05.300 --> 00:56:07.960
Looks like we've got another carnival on our hands.

00:56:09.060 --> 00:56:10.560
What on earth is this all about?!

00:56:14.490 --> 00:56:15.140
Inami-san.

00:56:15.790 --> 00:56:16.800
Look.

00:56:17.580 --> 00:56:18.820
Akkey!

00:56:18.820 --> 00:56:20.070
Hiro'omi?

00:56:20.070 --> 00:56:21.980
What are you guys doing here?

00:56:22.460 --> 00:56:23.920
We found these.

00:56:23.920 --> 00:56:25.290
The dreamshade!

00:56:28.410 --> 00:56:30.180
It's being sucked in.

00:56:32.710 --> 00:56:34.370
Let's hurry.

00:56:39.130 --> 00:56:41.570
Wait! Hold on a sec!

00:56:42.040 --> 00:56:42.740
No, get back!

00:56:42.740 --> 00:56:43.270
Is it a trap?
No, get back!

00:56:43.270 --> 00:56:43.750
Is it a trap?

00:56:43.750 --> 00:56:45.780
Just get back!

00:56:50.990 --> 00:56:51.880
Wh-What is...

00:56:52.310 --> 00:56:54.010
Stay away! This thing's dangerous!

00:56:57.880 --> 00:56:59.270
Wh-Whoops!

00:57:00.870 --> 00:57:01.970
What the hell are you doing?!

00:57:01.970 --> 00:57:03.480
This is no time to be messing around!

00:57:03.480 --> 00:57:04.850
What was that for?

00:57:04.850 --> 00:57:06.440
Here I'd made an amazing entrance—

00:57:07.580 --> 00:57:09.530
This is what you do after showing up
for the first time in forever?!

00:57:09.530 --> 00:57:11.010
Were you behind those letters as well?

00:57:11.010 --> 00:57:12.740
What were you being so roundabout for?

00:57:12.740 --> 00:57:13.340
You idiot!

00:57:13.340 --> 00:57:14.380
Who's that?

00:57:14.380 --> 00:57:16.280
Akkey's mother.

00:57:17.770 --> 00:57:18.490
Really?

00:57:18.920 --> 00:57:21.000
Is Kuriyama-san really alive?

00:57:21.700 --> 00:57:24.190
Yes, she's alive.

00:57:24.190 --> 00:57:26.850
Mirai-chan is fighting all by herself right now.

00:57:26.850 --> 00:57:28.810
I'm not supposed to be helping you out,

00:57:28.810 --> 00:57:32.370
but the world will end if the
shade beyond the horizon wins this battle.

00:57:32.370 --> 00:57:36.260
So I decided to consider this an emergency and act accordingly.

00:57:36.630 --> 00:57:39.220
Anyway, how can we save Kuriyama-san?

00:57:39.220 --> 00:57:42.270
Before we get to that, let me ask you something.

00:57:43.520 --> 00:57:46.520
Guys, do you wanna go to
where Kuriyama Mirai is—

00:57:48.020 --> 00:57:50.730
Lay off the nonsense and just tell us already!

00:57:50.730 --> 00:57:51.570
Okay, okay.

00:57:51.570 --> 00:57:53.440
Down there.

00:57:55.180 --> 00:57:56.820
A shadestone?

00:57:59.610 --> 00:58:01.120
What is this?

00:58:04.420 --> 00:58:05.080
Don't tell me...

00:58:05.560 --> 00:58:06.810
Right.

00:58:06.810 --> 00:58:08.330
This stone is a part of Akkun.

00:58:09.100 --> 00:58:13.550
In other words, it's also a part of
the shade from beyond the horizon.

00:58:33.860 --> 00:58:36.490
Inside that shade is something Kuriyama Mirai created:

00:58:37.220 --> 00:58:41.410
a puppet of Akihito formed by her intense emotions.

00:58:41.830 --> 00:58:44.410
Grab hold of it with everything you've got.

00:58:45.200 --> 00:58:47.920
That shadestone will do the rest.

00:58:48.620 --> 00:58:51.920
How do you know all this?

00:58:55.080 --> 00:58:56.280
Who do you think I am?

00:58:56.280 --> 00:58:59.430
I'm your mother—<i>the</i> Kanbara Yayoi.

00:59:04.760 --> 00:59:08.500
Someday you'll have to tell me all about myself. Got that?

00:59:11.940 --> 00:59:14.080
Jeez, that made me jump!

00:59:14.080 --> 00:59:15.200
Kanbara Yayoi!

00:59:15.200 --> 00:59:17.050
Don't scare me like that, Izumin!

00:59:17.050 --> 00:59:18.320
Now, hurry up and go!

00:59:18.320 --> 00:59:19.650
Wait.

00:59:19.650 --> 00:59:21.060
What do you plan to do
once you get there?

00:59:21.060 --> 00:59:22.070
You're no longer...

00:59:22.070 --> 00:59:23.580
...immortal.

00:59:25.210 --> 00:59:26.620
I know.

00:59:26.620 --> 00:59:32.840
But I'm still a pervert who's willing to do anything for the sake of glasses and bespectacled beauties!

00:59:32.840 --> 00:59:36.300
My cheeks are stained with tears

00:59:37.750 --> 00:59:40.340
Sorry to say this, but it's <i>our</i> turn now.

00:59:43.210 --> 00:59:46.100
How unusual for you to cave.

00:59:46.630 --> 00:59:47.640
Kanbara-senpai!

00:59:48.020 --> 00:59:50.130
Keep your dropkick ready and waiting!

00:59:50.130 --> 00:59:52.210
I'll bring her back for sure!

00:59:53.030 --> 00:59:53.940
Okay!

00:59:58.700 --> 01:00:01.060
Despite losing my way

01:00:01.060 --> 01:00:04.560
I continue to look for you

01:00:04.560 --> 01:00:09.900
My hands sense the thoughts you left behind

01:00:10.960 --> 01:00:16.160
I'll grab hold of you and never let go

01:00:16.160 --> 01:00:19.260
Two hearts seeking each other

01:00:19.260 --> 01:00:25.140
That's what dreams are made of

01:00:25.140 --> 01:00:30.770
Supporting one another draws us closer every time

01:00:30.770 --> 01:00:35.530
We don't need to live lives of sorrow anymore

01:00:35.530 --> 01:00:40.860
There's joy in supporting one another as you live

01:00:42.490 --> 01:00:43.780
Kuriyama-san!

01:00:45.410 --> 01:00:50.670
Will come to realize that

01:00:50.920 --> 01:00:53.260
Despite losing my way

01:00:53.260 --> 01:01:00.280
I found you

01:01:15.530 --> 01:01:17.310
Senpai?

01:01:21.900 --> 01:01:22.820
Kuriyama-san...

01:01:24.920 --> 01:01:26.570
Serves you right!

01:01:29.590 --> 01:01:31.130
Senpai?

01:01:31.130 --> 01:01:32.140
Why?

01:01:32.140 --> 01:01:33.250
Why did you come here?

01:01:33.250 --> 01:01:37.090
Now everything I did was in vain!

01:01:37.090 --> 01:01:38.210
Why do you think I—

01:01:38.210 --> 01:01:39.710
Shut up!

01:01:40.320 --> 01:01:42.390
"Live on"?

01:01:42.920 --> 01:01:45.970
"Become a normal person"?

01:01:45.970 --> 01:01:47.680
Who the hell wished for that?

01:01:47.680 --> 01:01:50.130
Who the hell asked for that crap?!

01:01:50.680 --> 01:01:52.400
How unpleasant!

01:01:52.400 --> 01:01:54.520
How utterly unpleasant!

01:01:54.520 --> 01:01:56.680
<i>I'm</i> the one who should be feeling unpleasant!

01:01:56.680 --> 01:01:58.190
Anyway, I refuse to stand for this!

01:01:58.790 --> 01:02:01.730
I don't want a life that was
built on your sacrifice.

01:02:01.730 --> 01:02:03.620
A future like that...

01:02:03.620 --> 01:02:04.820
holds no meaning at all!

01:02:05.640 --> 01:02:07.660
Why don't you understand that?!

01:02:08.660 --> 01:02:12.330
Why was that so difficult for you to understand?

01:02:23.140 --> 01:02:23.950
Jeez!

01:02:23.950 --> 01:02:26.260
How can anyone call that
absurd thing a dreamshade?

01:02:26.260 --> 01:02:27.240
Don't ask me!

01:02:27.240 --> 01:02:29.850
You were the one who was harboring it to begin with!

01:02:30.950 --> 01:02:32.400
That's just the core.

01:02:32.400 --> 01:02:35.750
In truth, everything around us was inside you.

01:02:41.940 --> 01:02:42.880
Senpai,

01:02:42.880 --> 01:02:43.900
have you come up with anything yet?

01:02:44.750 --> 01:02:45.760
What do you mean?

01:02:45.760 --> 01:02:47.200
Like a weakness or something!

01:02:47.200 --> 01:02:50.910
You know, maybe it has
sensitive armpits like you.

01:02:51.390 --> 01:02:52.990
Armpits?

01:02:53.450 --> 01:02:54.120
Where exactly?!

01:02:54.450 --> 01:02:57.820
Then... do you have something you hate?

01:02:57.820 --> 01:02:59.000
Anything will do.

01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:00.980
Something I hate, huh?

01:03:02.910 --> 01:03:04.090
Capelin with roe?

01:03:05.090 --> 01:03:09.050
Capelin with roe!

01:03:09.700 --> 01:03:10.800
Think it's mad now?

01:03:10.800 --> 01:03:11.930
Don't ask me!

01:03:24.360 --> 01:03:25.940
Kuriyama-san!

01:03:39.950 --> 01:03:41.850
Did you just do that?

01:03:41.850 --> 01:03:43.040
I think so.

01:03:43.710 --> 01:03:46.510
Wait, you have a shade hand now?

01:03:49.460 --> 01:03:55.360
That shadestone was a part of the
shade beyond the horizon—a part of you?

01:03:56.360 --> 01:04:00.810
Senpai, you hold a part of its powers in your hand right now!

01:04:01.540 --> 01:04:03.230
I'm not sure how we'll manage,

01:04:03.230 --> 01:04:07.070
but if you can stand up to it...

01:04:07.070 --> 01:04:10.550
...then it might be worth getting closer.

01:04:15.840 --> 01:04:17.330
On the handlebar?!

01:04:17.330 --> 01:04:19.620
There are dreamshades up ahead.

01:04:19.620 --> 01:04:21.160
From below, too!

01:04:27.920 --> 01:04:30.060
Way to go, Kuriyama-san!

01:04:30.060 --> 01:04:32.610
So do I just keep going straight?

01:04:32.610 --> 01:04:34.330
I don't know.

01:04:34.330 --> 01:04:36.220
But you better go as fast as you can!

01:04:36.830 --> 01:04:38.140
After all,

01:04:38.140 --> 01:04:41.440
it's too late to hit the brakes!

01:04:43.190 --> 01:04:44.690
Senpai!

01:05:01.240 --> 01:05:04.280
No way!

01:05:15.160 --> 01:05:16.600
Senpai!

01:05:22.730 --> 01:05:24.390
That was absurd.

01:05:24.390 --> 01:05:26.940
This whole place is absurd.

01:05:26.940 --> 01:05:28.050
In other words,

01:05:28.050 --> 01:05:29.600
you're absurd.

01:05:29.600 --> 01:05:30.190
Me?!

01:05:34.380 --> 01:05:36.280
Somehow we made it, though.

01:05:37.310 --> 01:05:38.380
Where are we?

01:05:39.630 --> 01:05:40.400
Huh?

01:05:43.580 --> 01:05:45.040
Our opponent's in a panic too.

01:05:45.040 --> 01:05:45.920
You can tell?

01:05:45.920 --> 01:05:47.510
I can't.

01:05:47.510 --> 01:05:50.440
But that's how I feel.

01:05:51.090 --> 01:05:52.920
I'm sure things will work out!

01:05:52.920 --> 01:05:55.430
That's kind of unlike you.

01:05:56.240 --> 01:05:58.330
I don't know what you're talking about.

01:05:59.020 --> 01:06:00.110
That said,

01:06:03.120 --> 01:06:04.770
I, Kuriyama Mirai,

01:06:04.770 --> 01:06:07.190
am feeling optimistic to an unpleasant degree!

01:06:33.800 --> 01:06:36.800
Go for it, Kuriyama-san!

01:07:06.150 --> 01:07:07.410
Kuriyama-san...

01:07:07.410 --> 01:07:08.790
Akkey...

01:07:15.560 --> 01:07:17.180
Kuriyama-san?

01:07:17.180 --> 01:07:17.970
Kuriyama-san.

01:07:18.830 --> 01:07:20.260
Kuriyama-san!

01:07:23.890 --> 01:07:25.270
Don't kill us.

01:07:25.270 --> 01:07:26.520
Disgusting.

01:07:26.520 --> 01:07:27.680
You monster.

01:07:27.680 --> 01:07:28.520
Don't kill us.

01:07:29.130 --> 01:07:30.770
Are these my memories?

01:07:32.440 --> 01:07:34.230
Senpai?

01:07:35.940 --> 01:07:37.670
Wh-What's going on?

01:07:38.360 --> 01:07:43.490
It's probably something similar to what showed up back in the Hollow Shadow.

01:07:43.490 --> 01:07:45.760
Close your eyes, Kuriyama-san.

01:07:46.290 --> 01:07:47.620
Just do it.

01:07:48.430 --> 01:07:49.000
Okay!

01:07:52.180 --> 01:07:53.570
Don't be swayed.

01:07:54.490 --> 01:08:00.530
They say that dreamshades are formed from the twisted human heart and the hatred within, right?

01:08:00.530 --> 01:08:04.620
Well, this is a manifestation of the weakness in our hearts.

01:08:05.470 --> 01:08:07.850
Didn't I tell you back when we first met?

01:08:08.660 --> 01:08:10.550
I told you that the same goes for me.

01:08:11.560 --> 01:08:14.020
I'm here by your side.

01:08:15.360 --> 01:08:17.020
We met each other.

01:08:17.940 --> 01:08:19.490
You're not alone anymore.

01:08:21.520 --> 01:08:22.490
Senpai!

01:08:23.620 --> 01:08:24.990
Open your eyes.

01:08:30.740 --> 01:08:32.620
W-What...

01:08:33.610 --> 01:08:34.920
The hell?

01:08:38.310 --> 01:08:39.330
Let's take them out.

01:08:40.200 --> 01:08:41.800
<i>All</i> of them?

01:08:41.800 --> 01:08:43.460
Do you have a better idea?

01:08:48.480 --> 01:08:49.920
How unpleasant.

01:09:54.870 --> 01:09:58.040
Did we get them all?

01:09:58.040 --> 01:09:59.210
Who knows?

01:10:05.740 --> 01:10:07.550
Pretty, isn't it?

01:10:09.210 --> 01:10:10.120
Y-Yeah.

01:10:17.590 --> 01:10:19.910
What are you so terrified of?

01:10:20.650 --> 01:10:22.180
It's okay.

01:10:22.180 --> 01:10:24.360
Every last bit of you is me.

01:10:25.310 --> 01:10:28.490
All of it used to be inside me.

01:10:29.290 --> 01:10:31.800
Including that sickening envy,

01:10:33.630 --> 01:10:36.920
the despair over the fact that I'll never be human,

01:10:36.920 --> 01:10:39.290
the sorrow of being abandoned,

01:10:39.290 --> 01:10:40.880
and the regret over hurting someone!

01:10:42.050 --> 01:10:43.050
Senpai...

01:10:43.050 --> 01:10:48.220
And the selfishness, doubt, hatred, resignation, pettiness, and self-preserving attitude!

01:10:49.720 --> 01:10:52.700
I won't let any of it outside!

01:10:52.700 --> 01:10:55.100
It all belongs to me!

01:10:55.100 --> 01:10:58.600
I'll be the one to carry it all!

01:11:00.430 --> 01:11:04.400
I'm the immortal half-shade, you know?

01:11:15.910 --> 01:11:17.840
Senpai...

01:11:28.150 --> 01:11:29.050
Senpai,

01:11:29.840 --> 01:11:32.580
could you come over here?

01:11:35.300 --> 01:11:36.310
I'm sorry.

01:11:37.260 --> 01:11:41.310
Er, um, uh...

01:11:41.310 --> 01:11:42.440
I have...

01:11:42.440 --> 01:11:44.440
a request...

01:11:46.180 --> 01:11:47.720
A request?

01:11:48.890 --> 01:11:49.990
Um...

01:11:50.890 --> 01:11:53.840
Please hold out your hand.

01:11:53.840 --> 01:11:54.700
My hand?

01:11:55.520 --> 01:11:56.470
Yes.

01:12:05.040 --> 01:12:06.590
Please pat my head.

01:12:07.210 --> 01:12:09.880
I want you to pat my head.

01:12:21.410 --> 01:12:22.440
Kuriyama-san...

01:12:23.440 --> 01:12:25.690
Say "thank you."

01:12:28.580 --> 01:12:30.040
Thank you.

01:12:30.040 --> 01:12:32.500
Say it like you mean it.

01:12:34.760 --> 01:12:35.830
Thank you.

01:12:41.610 --> 01:12:43.250
So happy...

01:12:44.610 --> 01:12:46.420
I'm so happy!

01:12:46.980 --> 01:12:48.380
Kuriyama-san!

01:12:48.960 --> 01:12:51.970
I'm so happy!

01:12:53.360 --> 01:12:55.450
Kuriyama-san, your legs...

01:12:55.450 --> 01:12:59.310
The shade beyond the horizon
has gone back to you,

01:13:00.120 --> 01:13:02.880
So this place will crumble away soon,

01:13:02.880 --> 01:13:04.690
and I'll probably disappear along with it.

01:13:06.000 --> 01:13:09.550
Now that it's gone back to you,

01:13:09.550 --> 01:13:12.300
I won't be able to exist.

01:13:12.300 --> 01:13:15.120
The real me is long gone, after all.

01:13:16.280 --> 01:13:19.490
I'm truly glad to have met you!

01:13:19.490 --> 01:13:20.040
Stop it!

01:13:20.040 --> 01:13:24.040
I'm truly glad to have fallen in love with you—

01:13:24.040 --> 01:13:25.460
Stop! Don't say it!

01:13:27.670 --> 01:13:30.960
Thank you so very much!

01:13:32.510 --> 01:13:34.130
Kuriyama-san!

01:13:34.130 --> 01:13:36.510
Hang on! This can't be happening!

01:13:36.510 --> 01:13:38.930
Kuriyama-san!

01:13:39.900 --> 01:13:42.020
Kuriyama-san!

01:13:58.180 --> 01:14:01.000
<i>Nobody knows if this was all predestined from the start,</i>

01:14:01.000 --> 01:14:04.580
<i>or if it only happened thanks to Kuriyama-san's efforts.</i>

01:14:05.600 --> 01:14:07.920
<i>But I definitely want to believe it was the latter.</i>

01:14:09.120 --> 01:14:12.380
<i>Anyway, the shade from beyond the horizon came back to me,</i>

01:14:12.970 --> 01:14:15.470
<i>and peace was restored to the world.</i>

01:14:15.470 --> 01:14:18.570
100 yen? Are you for real?!

01:14:18.570 --> 01:14:20.160
I'm off!

01:14:20.160 --> 01:14:22.060
Oh, morning!

01:14:22.060 --> 01:14:24.220
Good morning.

01:14:24.220 --> 01:14:25.390
Be careful out there.

01:14:25.390 --> 01:14:27.350
Sorry to keep you waiting.

01:14:27.350 --> 01:14:28.350
She dozed off!

01:14:30.130 --> 01:14:32.710
<i>Dreamshades exist as they always have,</i>

01:14:32.710 --> 01:14:37.030
<i>and spirit hunters make a living off them as </i>they<i> always have.</i>

01:14:37.030 --> 01:14:40.580
<i>Ayaka-san and Ai-chan went back to their place, too.</i>

01:14:42.210 --> 01:14:44.370
<i>Fujima Miroku went missing.</i>

01:14:44.370 --> 01:14:51.130
<i>One thing did change: Hiro'omi replaced Izumi-san as the head of the Nase family.</i>

01:14:51.130 --> 01:14:53.900
<i>But that didn't affect our lives much.</i>

01:14:53.900 --> 01:14:54.880
Nee-san...

01:14:55.840 --> 01:14:58.410
One day, you will also come to understand.

01:15:00.110 --> 01:15:01.270
Forgive me.

01:15:01.680 --> 01:15:05.680
<i>As usual, Mitsuki remains cooped up in the clubroom and showers me with verbal abuse.</i>

01:15:05.680 --> 01:15:11.940
If you know that good will prevail over evil in the end,
isn't it a waste of time to continue reading?

01:15:12.300 --> 01:15:15.040
That's what entertainment's all about, don't you think?

01:15:15.040 --> 01:15:16.440
Cut it out!

01:15:16.440 --> 01:15:19.280
Hey, it's only natural to keep one's hands warm in winter.

01:15:19.280 --> 01:15:21.080
There's nothing strange about what I'm doing.

01:15:21.080 --> 01:15:22.370
It's totally creepy-crawly!

01:15:22.370 --> 01:15:23.420
Three out of ten.

01:15:27.080 --> 01:15:29.870
<i>However, Kuriyama Mirai's no longer here.</i>

01:15:30.510 --> 01:15:34.310
<i>In the end, I lost.</i>

01:15:34.310 --> 01:15:38.510
<i>A future built on Kuriyama Mirai's sacrifice holds no meaning at all.</i>

01:15:39.460 --> 01:15:45.000
<i>That's what I yelled out back then, but here I am, having accepted—and living in—that very future.</i>

01:15:45.000 --> 01:15:48.190
<i>I'm sure this is what Kuriyama-san's saying right about now:</i>

01:15:48.190 --> 01:15:50.280
<i>"Serves you right."</i>

01:15:51.240 --> 01:15:52.730
How unpleasant.

01:15:57.940 --> 01:15:59.570
I...

01:16:00.170 --> 01:16:01.400
still have you.

01:16:08.080 --> 01:16:10.080
<i>Just as there is light even at night,</i>

01:16:10.750 --> 01:16:13.170
<i>just as there are shadows during the day,</i>

01:16:13.170 --> 01:16:16.420
<i>the world will never be free of darkness.</i>

01:16:16.420 --> 01:16:20.170
<i>At the same time, it will also never be overcome by it.</i>

01:16:20.790 --> 01:16:26.780
<i>Dyed in that half-baked hue, the universe will continue to move on and set events in motion.</i>

01:16:27.600 --> 01:16:30.520
<i>And in the midst of all that, I...</i>

01:16:46.450 --> 01:16:49.190
Tearing the silence to shreds

01:16:51.180 --> 01:16:52.790
U-Um...

01:16:55.580 --> 01:16:56.840
Bespectacled...

01:16:57.970 --> 01:16:58.270
My eyes filled with regret, I see you

01:16:58.270 --> 01:17:02.870
Basically, I love the bespectacled Kuriyama-san!
My eyes filled with regret, I see you

01:17:02.870 --> 01:17:03.590
Basically, I love the bespectacled Kuriyama-san!

01:17:05.610 --> 01:17:09.190
Blossoming beautifully

01:17:09.640 --> 01:17:13.810
I can see the flower bringing joy to people's lives

01:17:16.630 --> 01:17:18.150
How unpleasant.

01:17:18.150 --> 01:17:21.000
<i>Nobody knows if this was all predestined from the start,</i>

01:17:21.000 --> 01:17:24.740
<i>or if it only happened thanks to Kuriyama-san's efforts.</i>

01:17:24.740 --> 01:17:29.240
<i>Maybe my feelings for Kuriyama-san reached her.</i>

01:17:29.240 --> 01:17:32.920
<i>And that's how I reunited with Kuriyama Mirai.</i>

01:17:32.920 --> 01:17:37.190
<i>If our story had ended after a reunion like that,</i>

01:17:37.190 --> 01:17:41.130
<i>I don't think any story in this world would be worth telling.</i>

01:17:41.520 --> 01:17:44.140
Oh right, Kuriyama-san.

01:17:44.140 --> 01:17:45.750
You forgot something.

01:17:46.190 --> 01:17:49.720
I have never said goodbye

01:17:51.150 --> 01:17:55.140
Could you do me a favor and put these glasses on?

01:18:02.940 --> 01:18:06.160
Continuing crystallization of proof

01:18:06.160 --> 01:18:08.820
Sheltering a faintly flickering flame

01:18:08.820 --> 01:18:10.960
Emblazoned with a future radiating brilliance

01:18:10.960 --> 01:18:14.470
Your eyes seem to hold a little bit of sadness

01:18:14.470 --> 01:18:17.230
Take a look into my eyes

01:18:17.230 --> 01:18:20.160
Wipe away that final tear

01:18:20.160 --> 01:18:22.880
Every time you wanna see me, call me

01:18:22.880 --> 01:18:25.770
I’ll be at the place where we first met

01:18:25.770 --> 01:18:30.000
Fight against the fate that befalls you

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:35.950
Yeah, bloom vibrantly, with glory

01:18:35.950 --> 01:18:38.590
Always

01:18:39.600 --> 01:18:45.200
Connected to your singing voice

01:18:45.200 --> 01:18:50.860
My sound rings out and echoes deep within my heart

01:18:50.860 --> 01:18:56.560
The tomorrow that surfaces in my prayer

01:18:56.560 --> 01:19:01.920
Transforms a reason to live into hope

01:19:02.230 --> 01:19:06.550
I wanna be with you

01:19:07.020 --> 01:19:09.800
To make a sacrifice to gain possession of

01:19:09.800 --> 01:19:12.410
This present reality, impossible to repeat

01:19:12.410 --> 01:19:15.200
The act is unbreakably bound to loneliness

01:19:15.200 --> 01:19:17.280
I can’t measure that weight as I am now

01:19:17.280 --> 01:19:19.040
But even so, that’s fine

01:19:19.040 --> 01:19:21.850
Echo far and wide, my prayer

01:19:21.850 --> 01:19:25.310
Our reverberating singing voices

01:19:25.310 --> 01:19:27.910
Painted a momentary light

01:19:27.910 --> 01:19:30.760
Illuminating a single flower

01:19:30.760 --> 01:19:34.240
I want to keep our hands connected

01:19:34.240 --> 01:19:36.430
And always be with you

01:20:36.910 --> 01:20:38.390
<i>I can't hear you...</i>

01:20:46.110 --> 01:20:47.670
<i>I can't hear you...</i>

01:21:06.670 --> 01:21:08.710
<i>Who...</i>

01:21:16.120 --> 01:21:17.430
Kuriyama-san?

01:21:20.970 --> 01:21:22.440
Who...

01:21:22.440 --> 01:21:23.940
Am I?

01:21:30.730 --> 01:21:31.240
Kuriyama-

01:21:31.240 --> 01:21:31.630
Who...
Kuriyama-

01:21:31.630 --> 01:21:32.400
Who...

01:21:34.450 --> 01:21:35.910
Are you?

01:21:37.200 --> 01:21:38.670
Kuriyama-san...
